-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) -- s.44 quiet enjoyment and s.46
-- lessor's right of entry. Based on content from the Western Australian
-- Legislation website at 2026-09-07, "Residential Tenancies Act 1987",
-- State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0.

§ `Part IV - Residential tenancy agreements`

§§ `Division 2 - General standard terms`

§§§ `44. Quiet enjoyment`

DECLARE `quiet enjoyment facts` HAS
    `the tenant's quiet enjoyment of the premises is interrupted by the lessor or any person claiming by, through or under the lessor or having superior title to that of the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor causes or permits any interference with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of the tenant in the use by the tenant of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any other tenant of the lessor in occupation of adjacent premises causes or permits any interference with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of the tenant in the use by the tenant of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has taken all reasonable steps to enforce the obligation of any other tenant of the lessor in occupation of adjacent premises` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.44
@export Decide whether the lessor is in breach of the quiet enjoyment term in s.44(2)
GIVEN facts IS A `quiet enjoyment facts` @desc Facts about interruption of quiet enjoyment and interference with the tenant's reasonable peace, comfort or privacy, including by another tenant of the lessor in adjacent premises and whether the lessor has taken all reasonable steps to enforce that other tenant's obligation.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor is in breach of the quiet enjoyment term` IF
        facts's `the tenant's quiet enjoyment of the premises is interrupted by the lessor or any person claiming by, through or under the lessor or having superior title to that of the lessor`
    OR  facts's `the lessor causes or permits any interference with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of the tenant in the use by the tenant of the premises`
    OR  (
            facts's `any other tenant of the lessor in occupation of adjacent premises causes or permits any interference with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of the tenant in the use by the tenant of the premises`
        AND NOT facts's `the lessor has taken all reasonable steps to enforce the obligation of any other tenant of the lessor in occupation of adjacent premises`
        )

§§§ `46. Lessor's right of entry`

-- Hour of proposed entry is 0-23 in the local time of the premises.
-- 8 means 8.00 a.m.; 18 means 6.00 p.m.

DECLARE `proposed entry` HAS
    `the proposed entry is on a weekday` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proposed entry is on a Saturday` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hour of proposed entry` IS A NUMBER
    `the time is agreed between the lessor and each tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entry is in any case of emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entry is for conducting a routine inspection of the premises or any other purpose under section 46(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of written notice before the proposed entry` IS A NUMBER
    `inspections of the premises under section 46(2)(b) in the 12 month period including this entry` IS A NUMBER
    `the entry is at any reasonable time for the purpose of collecting the rent under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rent is payable not more frequently than once every week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is agreed that the rent be collected at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entry is under section 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entry is for the purpose of carrying out or inspecting necessary repairs to or maintenance of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours of written notice before the proposed entry` IS A NUMBER
    `the entry is for the purpose of showing the premises to prospective tenants` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entry is during the period of 21 days preceding the termination of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has been given reasonable notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of occasions the premises have been shown including this entry is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entry is for the purpose of showing the premises to prospective purchasers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entry is for inspecting the premises and assessing any damage after termination of a tenant's interest under section 60(1)(ba) or (bb)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after receiving notice under section 71AB(1) or 71AD(4)` IS A NUMBER
    `days of notice to each tenant of the lessor's intention to enter` IS A NUMBER
    `the entry is for inspecting the premises and assessing any damage after termination of a tenant's interest under section 60(1)(bc)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days before the hearing of the application under section 71AE` IS A NUMBER
    `the tenant's consent is given at or immediately before the time of entry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice specifies the day of the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice specifies whether the entry will be before or after 12.00 p.m. on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it would unduly inconvenience the tenant for the lessor to enter as specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has made a reasonable attempt to negotiate a day and time that does not unduly inconvenience the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor would exercise the right of entry in a reasonable manner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `without the tenant's consent the lessor would stay or permit others to stay longer than is necessary to achieve the purpose of the entry` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed entry is at a reasonable time` IF
        entry's `the time is agreed between the lessor and each tenant`
    OR  (
            entry's `the proposed entry is on a weekday`
        AND entry's `hour of proposed entry` AT LEAST 8
        AND entry's `hour of proposed entry` AT MOST 18
        )
    OR  (
            entry's `the proposed entry is on a Saturday`
        AND entry's `hour of proposed entry` AT LEAST 9
        AND entry's `hour of proposed entry` AT MOST 17
        )

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 46(2)(b) applies` IF
        entry's `the entry is for conducting a routine inspection of the premises or any other purpose under section 46(2)(b)`
    AND `the proposed entry is at a reasonable time` entry
    AND entry's `days of written notice before the proposed entry` AT LEAST 7
    AND entry's `days of written notice before the proposed entry` AT MOST 14
    AND entry's `the notice specifies the day of the entry`
    AND entry's `the notice specifies whether the entry will be before or after 12.00 p.m. on that day`
    AND (
            NOT entry's `it would unduly inconvenience the tenant for the lessor to enter as specified in the notice`
        OR  entry's `the lessor has made a reasonable attempt to negotiate a day and time that does not unduly inconvenience the tenant`
        )

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 46(2)(c) applies` IF
        entry's `the entry is at any reasonable time for the purpose of collecting the rent under the agreement`
    AND `the proposed entry is at a reasonable time` entry
    AND entry's `the rent is payable not more frequently than once every week`
    AND entry's `it is agreed that the rent be collected at the premises`

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 46(2)(e) applies` IF
        entry's `the entry is for the purpose of carrying out or inspecting necessary repairs to or maintenance of the premises`
    AND `the proposed entry is at a reasonable time` entry
    AND entry's `hours of written notice before the proposed entry` AT LEAST 72

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 46(2)(f) applies` IF
        entry's `the entry is for the purpose of showing the premises to prospective tenants`
    AND `the proposed entry is at a reasonable time` entry
    AND entry's `the entry is during the period of 21 days preceding the termination of the agreement`
    AND entry's `the tenant has been given reasonable notice in writing`
    AND entry's `the number of occasions the premises have been shown including this entry is reasonable`

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 46(2)(g) applies` IF
        entry's `the entry is for the purpose of showing the premises to prospective purchasers`
    AND `the proposed entry is at a reasonable time` entry
    AND entry's `the tenant has been given reasonable notice in writing`
    AND entry's `the number of occasions the premises have been shown including this entry is reasonable`

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 46(2)(ga)(i) applies` IF
        entry's `the entry is for inspecting the premises and assessing any damage after termination of a tenant's interest under section 60(1)(ba) or (bb)`
    AND entry's `days after receiving notice under section 71AB(1) or 71AD(4)` AT MOST 7
    AND entry's `days of notice to each tenant of the lessor's intention to enter` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 46(2)(ga)(ii) applies` IF
        entry's `the entry is for inspecting the premises and assessing any damage after termination of a tenant's interest under section 60(1)(bc)`
    AND entry's `days before the hearing of the application under section 71AE` AT MOST 10
    AND entry's `days of notice to each tenant of the lessor's intention to enter` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a circumstance in section 46(2) applies` IF
        entry's `the entry is in any case of emergency`
    OR  `section 46(2)(b) applies` entry
    OR  `section 46(2)(c) applies` entry
    OR  entry's `the entry is under section 77(4)`
    OR  `section 46(2)(e) applies` entry
    OR  `section 46(2)(f) applies` entry
    OR  `section 46(2)(g) applies` entry
    OR  `section 46(2)(ga)(i) applies` entry
    OR  `section 46(2)(ga)(ii) applies` entry
    OR  entry's `the tenant's consent is given at or immediately before the time of entry`

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inspection frequency limit in section 46(3) is exceeded` IF
        entry's `the entry is for conducting a routine inspection of the premises or any other purpose under section 46(2)(b)`
    AND entry's `inspections of the premises under section 46(2)(b) in the 12 month period including this entry` GREATER THAN 4

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.46
@export Decide whether the lessor may enter the premises under s.46
GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry` @desc A proposed entry. Hour of proposed entry is 0-23 local time (8 = 8.00 a.m., 18 = 6.00 p.m.). Reasonable time is 8.00 a.m. to 6.00 p.m. on a weekday, 9.00 a.m. to 5.00 p.m. on a Saturday, or a time agreed with each tenant. For a routine inspection, written notice must be at least 7 and at most 14 days before, and not more than 4 inspections in any 12 month period. For repairs, at least 72 hours written notice. Also whether the lessor would enter in a reasonable manner and not stay longer than necessary.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor may enter the premises` IF
        `a circumstance in section 46(2) applies` entry
    AND NOT `the inspection frequency limit in section 46(3) is exceeded` entry
    AND entry's `the lessor would exercise the right of entry in a reasonable manner`
    AND NOT entry's `without the tenant's consent the lessor would stay or permit others to stay longer than is necessary to achieve the purpose of the entry`

GIVEN entry IS A `proposed entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant is entitled to be on the premises during the entry` IF
        `section 46(2)(f) applies` entry
    OR  `section 46(2)(g) applies` entry

§§ `Fixtures`

`neighbour noise lessor took no steps` MEANS `quiet enjoyment facts` WITH
    `the tenant's quiet enjoyment of the premises is interrupted by the lessor or any person claiming by, through or under the lessor or having superior title to that of the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor causes or permits any interference with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of the tenant in the use by the tenant of the premises` IS FALSE,
    `any other tenant of the lessor in occupation of adjacent premises causes or permits any interference with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of the tenant in the use by the tenant of the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor has taken all reasonable steps to enforce the obligation of any other tenant of the lessor in occupation of adjacent premises` IS FALSE

`neighbour noise lessor enforced` MEANS `quiet enjoyment facts` WITH
    `the tenant's quiet enjoyment of the premises is interrupted by the lessor or any person claiming by, through or under the lessor or having superior title to that of the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor causes or permits any interference with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of the tenant in the use by the tenant of the premises` IS FALSE,
    `any other tenant of the lessor in occupation of adjacent premises causes or permits any interference with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of the tenant in the use by the tenant of the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor has taken all reasonable steps to enforce the obligation of any other tenant of the lessor in occupation of adjacent premises` IS TRUE

`weekday emergency at 10` MEANS `proposed entry` WITH
    `the proposed entry is on a weekday` IS TRUE,
    `the proposed entry is on a Saturday` IS FALSE,
    `hour of proposed entry` IS 10,
    `the time is agreed between the lessor and each tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is in any case of emergency` IS TRUE,
    `the entry is for conducting a routine inspection of the premises or any other purpose under section 46(2)(b)` IS FALSE,
    `days of written notice before the proposed entry` IS 0,
    `inspections of the premises under section 46(2)(b) in the 12 month period including this entry` IS 0,
    `the entry is at any reasonable time for the purpose of collecting the rent under the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the rent is payable not more frequently than once every week` IS FALSE,
    `it is agreed that the rent be collected at the premises` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is under section 77(4)` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is for the purpose of carrying out or inspecting necessary repairs to or maintenance of the premises` IS FALSE,
    `hours of written notice before the proposed entry` IS 0,
    `the entry is for the purpose of showing the premises to prospective tenants` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is during the period of 21 days preceding the termination of the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant has been given reasonable notice in writing` IS FALSE,
    `the number of occasions the premises have been shown including this entry is reasonable` IS TRUE,
    `the entry is for the purpose of showing the premises to prospective purchasers` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is for inspecting the premises and assessing any damage after termination of a tenant's interest under section 60(1)(ba) or (bb)` IS FALSE,
    `days after receiving notice under section 71AB(1) or 71AD(4)` IS 0,
    `days of notice to each tenant of the lessor's intention to enter` IS 0,
    `the entry is for inspecting the premises and assessing any damage after termination of a tenant's interest under section 60(1)(bc)` IS FALSE,
    `days before the hearing of the application under section 71AE` IS 0,
    `the tenant's consent is given at or immediately before the time of entry` IS FALSE,
    `the notice specifies the day of the entry` IS FALSE,
    `the notice specifies whether the entry will be before or after 12.00 p.m. on that day` IS FALSE,
    `it would unduly inconvenience the tenant for the lessor to enter as specified in the notice` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has made a reasonable attempt to negotiate a day and time that does not unduly inconvenience the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor would exercise the right of entry in a reasonable manner` IS TRUE,
    `without the tenant's consent the lessor would stay or permit others to stay longer than is necessary to achieve the purpose of the entry` IS FALSE

`fifth weekday inspection with 7 days notice` MEANS `proposed entry` WITH
    `the proposed entry is on a weekday` IS TRUE,
    `the proposed entry is on a Saturday` IS FALSE,
    `hour of proposed entry` IS 10,
    `the time is agreed between the lessor and each tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is in any case of emergency` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is for conducting a routine inspection of the premises or any other purpose under section 46(2)(b)` IS TRUE,
    `days of written notice before the proposed entry` IS 7,
    `inspections of the premises under section 46(2)(b) in the 12 month period including this entry` IS 5,
    `the entry is at any reasonable time for the purpose of collecting the rent under the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the rent is payable not more frequently than once every week` IS FALSE,
    `it is agreed that the rent be collected at the premises` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is under section 77(4)` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is for the purpose of carrying out or inspecting necessary repairs to or maintenance of the premises` IS FALSE,
    `hours of written notice before the proposed entry` IS 0,
    `the entry is for the purpose of showing the premises to prospective tenants` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is during the period of 21 days preceding the termination of the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant has been given reasonable notice in writing` IS FALSE,
    `the number of occasions the premises have been shown including this entry is reasonable` IS TRUE,
    `the entry is for the purpose of showing the premises to prospective purchasers` IS FALSE,
    `the entry is for inspecting the premises and assessing any damage after termination of a tenant's interest under section 60(1)(ba) or (bb)` IS FALSE,
    `days after receiving notice under section 71AB(1) or 71AD(4)` IS 0,
    `days of notice to each tenant of the lessor's intention to enter` IS 0,
    `the entry is for inspecting the premises and assessing any damage after termination of a tenant's interest under section 60(1)(bc)` IS FALSE,
    `days before the hearing of the application under section 71AE` IS 0,
    `the tenant's consent is given at or immediately before the time of entry` IS FALSE,
    `the notice specifies the day of the entry` IS TRUE,
    `the notice specifies whether the entry will be before or after 12.00 p.m. on that day` IS TRUE,
    `it would unduly inconvenience the tenant for the lessor to enter as specified in the notice` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has made a reasonable attempt to negotiate a day and time that does not unduly inconvenience the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor would exercise the right of entry in a reasonable manner` IS TRUE,
    `without the tenant's consent the lessor would stay or permit others to stay longer than is necessary to achieve the purpose of the entry` IS FALSE

#EVAL `the lessor is in breach of the quiet enjoyment term` `neighbour noise lessor took no steps`
#EVAL `the lessor is in breach of the quiet enjoyment term` `neighbour noise lessor enforced`
#EVAL `the lessor may enter the premises` `weekday emergency at 10`
#EVAL `the lessor may enter the premises` `fifth weekday inspection with 7 days notice`
#ASSERT `the lessor is in breach of the quiet enjoyment term` `neighbour noise lessor took no steps` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the lessor is in breach of the quiet enjoyment term` `neighbour noise lessor enforced` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the lessor may enter the premises` `weekday emergency at 10` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the lessor may enter the premises` `fifth weekday inspection with 7 days notice` EQUALS FALSE
